==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{der|fo|non|góðr}}, from {{der|fo|gem-pro|*gōdaz}}, from {{der|fo|ine-pro|*gʰedʰ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|fo|/ˈkɔuːwʊɹ/}}
*: {{rhymes|fo|ɔuːwʊɹ}}

===Adjective===
{{fo-adj|betri|bestur}}

# [[good]]
#* Genesis 1:31 ([http://www.biblian.fo/default.asp?gerd=visbok&bokid=1&kapitulid=1 Faroese Bible])
#*: ''Og Gud sá alt tað, ið Hann hevði gjørt - og tað var sera gott. Og kvøld varð, og morgun varð, sætta dag.''
#*:: God saw all that he had made, and it was very '''good'''. And there was evening, and there was morning—the sixth day.

====Declension====
{{fo-decl-adj-16|g|ó|o}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|fo|ringur}}, {{l|fo|illur}} (bad)

